WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:05.810
Jumanji: The Next Level is packed with action
and jokes, with plenty to keep even the child

00:00:05.810 --> 00:00:07.820
with the shortest attention span happy.

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:13.220
There's also plenty of stuff to keep older
viewers engaged... and asking questions.

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:19.660
These are some of things that only adult moviegoers
will notice in Jumanji: The Next Level but

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:21.900
beware: there are spoilers ahead!

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:26.960
It's hard not to wonder who Jumanji: The Next
Level thinks its audience is.

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:29.160
The film's marketed as a family film.

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:34.380
After all, its central protagonists are teenagers
and the action revolves around a video game

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:37.520
with lots of jokes and action sequences to
fill out the running time.

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:43.210
There's a romantic subplot involving Martha
and Spencer, two warring friends resolve their

00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:46.540
differences, and every character learns a
little about themselves.

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:51.520
Yes, like its predecessor, there's a little
something for everybody in Jumanji: The Next

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:53.220
Level — a little too much.

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:58.020
Kid viewers may marvel at the dazzling array
of treats on offer, but adults may be puzzled

00:00:58.020 --> 00:01:00.840
as to who, exactly, this movie is for.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:05.800
It's a kids' movie, but the kids in it are
college-age, so then they're actually adults.

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:10.920
Coming to terms with aging is a major theme
— Danny DeVito's Eddie learns that growing

00:01:10.930 --> 00:01:15.910
old isn't a burden but rather "a gift" and
he goes back into the workforce after 15 years

00:01:15.910 --> 00:01:18.760
of fuming over his business partner selling
his restaurant.

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:24.120
That's not exactly something kids can relate
to, but then, older adult viewers who would

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:28.310
get all that probably don't care too much
about the inner workings of video games.

00:01:29.310 --> 00:01:33.750
It takes a while for Jumanji: The Next Level
to get going, which is to say to get the young

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:38.700
quartet of friends into the video game world
and into the skins of their movie star avatars.

00:01:39.190 --> 00:01:44.340
The long first act of the movie catches up
the audience on what Bethany, Spencer, Fridge,

00:01:44.340 --> 00:01:48.660
and Martha have been up to since last they
were seen in Jumanji: Welcome to the Jungle.

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:53.800
In short, they've all graduated high school
and moved away Martha is in college, Fridge

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:59.250
is too, Bethany does charity work, and Spencer
works a dreary job in a Manhattan pharmacy.

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:03.540
They all reconnect when they come home for
the holidays, or at least they try to.

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:05.200
You still talking to your friends?"

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:06.260
"It's complicated.

00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:10.580
When we first got together, we were different
people."

00:02:10.590 --> 00:02:15.380
Spencer doesn't show up for a scheduled brunch,
and the other three realize he's been increasingly

00:02:15.380 --> 00:02:16.880
out of touch in recent months.

00:02:17.220 --> 00:02:22.260
This is a pattern older viewers know all too
well: One naturally grows apart from their

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:24.800
tight circle of high school and hometown friends.

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:30.060
Kid viewers may not quite understand or believe
that they won't be best friends forever with

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:35.471
their childhood BFFs, but Jumanji: The Next
Level makes it clear why that happens: These

00:02:35.471 --> 00:02:39.631
four people, who live in different parts of
the country following different paths, don't

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:41.460
have very much in common with each other.

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:47.140
On the surface, it's a movie about video games
and celebrity impersonations, but Jumanji:

00:02:47.140 --> 00:02:52.620
The Next Level surprisingly — and effectively
— explores a number of psychological truths,

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:56.680
most of which kids just wouldn't understand
because they simply haven't lived long enough

00:02:56.680 --> 00:02:57.240
to relate.

00:02:57.760 --> 00:03:02.180
Spencer is full-on depressed — he feels
like his life is going nowhere and because

00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:05.420
of that, is too ashamed to see his more successful
friends.

00:03:05.860 --> 00:03:09.400
It's a mindset that already led him to split
with his girlfriend, Martha.

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:14.260
Many people have this type of existential
crisis after high school, the sense of not

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:18.580
knowing what to do or where to go next and
feeling like a failure because of it.

00:03:18.820 --> 00:03:24.480
Particularly astute audience members may think
that Spencer feels he "peaked" already — after

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:28.300
all, he's likely never going to have a life
experience that comes close to matching living

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:29.930
inside of a deadly video game.

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:36.040
Rory McCann joins the world of Jumanji with
his role as the terrifying villain of Jumanji:

00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:41.880
The Next Level, a power-mad, aptly-named warrior-king
named Jurgen the Brutal.

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:46.440
McCann is most recognizable to audiences — and
primarily to the adults in the audience for

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:51.220
his work on Game of Thrones as the equally
intimidating Sandor Clegane, a.k.a.

00:03:51.220 --> 00:03:52.080
"The Hound."

00:03:52.440 --> 00:03:54.420
"You don't seem to understand the situation."

00:03:54.430 --> 00:04:00.560
"I understand that if any more words come
pouring out of your c--- mouth, I'm going

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:02.260
to have to eat every f------ chicken in this
room."

00:04:02.420 --> 00:04:07.060
Jurgen the Brutal ultimately isn't all that
far removed from the Hound, as Jumanji: The

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:11.520
Next Level includes a few clever references
to McCann's late, great HBO series.

00:04:11.820 --> 00:04:16.900
Early in the film, Jurgen is flanked by a
pair of massive, bloodthirsty hyenas.

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:22.539
They're very shaggy, and not instantly recognizable
as that particular wild animal; they actually

00:04:22.540 --> 00:04:26.560
look more like big dogs, or, in Thrones parlance,
direwolves.

00:04:27.020 --> 00:04:31.479
Dressed in furs and sulking around a castle
half the time, Jurgen sometimes looks like

00:04:31.479 --> 00:04:36.479
he's cosplaying as Jon Snow, but then the
film gives a shout-out to his old Game of

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:37.380
Thrones character.

00:04:37.900 --> 00:04:42.100
Jurgen battles to the death with Dr. Smolder
Bravestone on an airship.

00:04:42.220 --> 00:04:46.600
At one point, Bravestone jumps onto Jurgen,
sending them both falling.

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:50.979
That's just like the way the Hound jumped
onto his brother, the Mountain, during their

00:04:50.979 --> 00:04:53.620
epic battle that resulted in both of their
deaths.

00:04:53.620 --> 00:04:56.689
Jumanji: The Next Level is dark and full of
terrors.

00:04:57.949 --> 00:05:02.590
From video games to quality television, kids
have a variety of entertainment options at

00:05:02.590 --> 00:05:06.900
their disposal, but at the end of the day,
most all of them are going to wind up watching

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:13.030
the same movie, a true classic fervently beloved
by all the children of the world in the year

00:05:13.030 --> 00:05:20.539
2019: Lawrence of Arabia, the 1962 historical
epic about British military leader T.E. Lawrence

00:05:20.540 --> 00:05:23.009
that won the Academy Award for Best Picture.

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:28.580
Yeah, no, we're totally kidding — kids today
aren't into Lawrence of Arabia, nor were kids

00:05:28.580 --> 00:05:30.440
into the movie when it was first released.

00:05:30.740 --> 00:05:35.879
However, it's an indelible classic of film,
and at least two of its elements became cultural

00:05:35.879 --> 00:05:42.119
touchstones: cinematographer Freddie Young's
sweeping, beautiful shots of desert landscapes,

00:05:42.120 --> 00:05:44.860
and Maurice Jarre's regal, rousing score.

00:05:45.260 --> 00:05:50.240
Jumanji: The Next Level features many desert
scenes, providing the opportunity for a visual

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:54.100
reference to Lawrence of Arabia in the form
of an extra-wide shot.

00:05:54.100 --> 00:05:58.960
More mature filmgoers will likely understand
these allusions, especially since the Jumanji

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:03.040
score emphasizes it with musical motifs that
hint at the Lawrence score.

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:08.100
There are very few kids on Earth who would
smile and chuckle at these highbrow references.

